// dna/tests/graph_model_test.hl — the repository as one hypergraph in the
// record, projected into memory (GH #1085).
//
// The record is written with the graph voice's GRAPH.md lists "as they
// stand" — the nodes and the hyperedges — plus its holes filled as its org
// chart renders them (a board, a dev and a reviewer under every process,
// an operator under every deployment, who holds them and what they sign),
// and three of its practices as
// knowledge ideas, two of them ratified and bound. The tail projects it,
// and memory answers with GRAPH.md's counts and both perspectives: the
// org chart and the process model. A row re-put replaces its edge's
// members, a retired one leaves (a retired node leaves the perspectives),
// a rebuild reproduces both perspectives, and a malformed one stops the projection
// at its row with the reason. The checks on rows run without memory;
// memory is Postgres, and without the owner's DSN in
// HALE_DNA_MEMORY_DSN_OWNER the projection half is not exercised.

import "../core" as dna;
import "../operations" as ops;

// GRAPH.md at hale-lang/voice 2b1cb565 (hale-lang/voice#3, the commit
// #1090 vendors), "The nodes, as they stand" and "The edges, as they
// stand", one row per line: `N|kind|name|text` or `E|kind|role=node|…|
// via=…|outside=…`. Practices are not here: they are knowledge ideas
// (below), and the constrains edge of "Only the api is exposed", which
// names one, is written beside them.
